# Eine kleine Nachtmusik, the opening (repertoire plan: eine-kleine-nachtmusik). The first four
# bars of the Serenade in G, K. 525, first movement, where the whole orchestra plays the same notes:
# the call G D G D, the rising G major arpeggio G D G B D, then the answer C A C A and C A F# A D,
# which outlines D7. All first position: open strings 3, 4 and 2, string 2 fret 3 (D) and fret 1
# (C), string 3 fret 2 (A), string 4 fret 4 (F#). Every rest is part of the music.
title: Eine kleine Nachtmusik (opening)
id: eine-kleine-nachtmusik
composer: Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart
source: Serenade No. 13 in G, K. 525 (1787), first movement, bars 1-4; arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (Mozart died in 1791); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 3
tags: mozart, classical, arpeggio, rests
tempo: 96
time: 4/4
key: G

track: Melody
role: lead
